            <ArticleTitle>Chronic daily headache: is &quot;cervicogenic headache&quot; one subgroup?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>&quot;Chronic daily headache&quot; should not include cervicogenic headache, which in its typical form is a unilateral headache that can be precipitated mechanically; in other words, probably an organic disorder. Chronic daily headache as such should not be included in the IHS classification.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
